Vim-HackerNews Changelog
========================


Version 0.3-dev
---------------

- Switch to the official Hacker News Firebase API for all requests
  (stories/items/comments); remove dependency on third-party API
- Add progress messages while fetching stories/items/comments
- Add option `g:hackernews_show_progress` (default: on)
- Speed: parallelize story detail fetches with configurable concurrency
  (`g:hackernews_concurrency`, default 12) and configurable max items per list
  (`g:hackernews_max_items`).
  Implementation: a bounded worker pool fetches item JSON concurrently, results
  are reassembled in order, and periodic progress messages are emitted.
- Prefer Vim's Python 3 provider when available to improve TLS reliability
- Add `:HackerNewsRefresh` command to clear and refetch the active story list
- Add Python unit tests plus coverage configuration for the Hacker News module
- Improve Python 3 reloading compatibility
- Update docs to reflect supported lists (top, ask, show, jobs, best, newest)
  and remove references to deprecated lists (active, shownew, noobstories)


Version 0.2
-----------

Released April 26, 2015

- Add Python 3 support
- Add additional motions to improve browsing of story lists, comments, articles
- Add comment thread folding
- Add ability to display specific HackerNews lists (top, ask, show, etc)
- Handle all HackerNews item types properly (poll, job, etc)
- Save cursor position when moving back/forward
- Add highlighting of OP username in comment titles
- Do not load python code until first :HackerNews command
- Timeout HTTP requests after 5 seconds instead of hanging Vim
- Improve HTTP error information
- Add units tests with Vader.vim
- Add Travis CI integration
- Lots of syntax fixes and improvements
- Dozens of other bug fixes and improvements


Version 0.1.1
-------------

Released February 7, 2015

- Fix "job" type items without a `domain` key in API


Version 0.1
-----------

Released February 7, 2015

- Initial release
